'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  e7-next-hub-instruction-test.spin2
''   Purpose....  Erratum E7 test: whether a RDLONG or WRLONG issued 0 to
''                8 instructions after a no-wait RDFAST completes before
''                its own hub access, in every hub alignment; the waiting
''                form alongside; and whether making the first of two
''                RDFASTs the waiting form removes E7's original failure
''   Manual.....  P2 Errata
''   Version....  v0.2.0 (2026-09-26)
''   Appears in.  Erratum E7: After a No-Wait RDFAST, the Next Hub
''                Instruction Can Complete Early; Appendix A: The Test
''                Programs
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. It is the whole
''   program the chapters listed above name; where the manual
''   quotes it, it quotes excerpts.
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS MEASURED

  Erratum E7: after a no-wait RDFAST (D[31] = 1), the next hub
  instruction can complete early.  This program measures two things.

  1. A RDLONG or WRLONG issued 0 to 8 instructions after a no-wait RDFAST.
     Predicted when it completes early:
      - A RDLONG writes its destination with the long of the PREVIOUS
        slow hub read (here: the primer, $A5A5_0001), not the long at its
        own address (the sentinel, $5A5A_0002).
      - A WRLONG completes before its write lands; a hub-memory
        instruction issued next can then cancel the write.
      - The waiting form (D[31] = 0) does neither.
     Whether the following RDLONG completes early depends on the hub-slot
     alignment of the two addresses, so every run sweeps all 8 x 8
     (af, ar) slot-bit pairs.

  2. Two RDFASTs in a row.  A blocking RDFAST issued 8..15 clocks after a
     no-wait RDFAST, at the one spacing the alignment selects, takes 2
     clocks and the next RFLONG reads $0000_0000.  Arm E7N reproduces
     this (positive control); arm E7B is identical with the first RDFAST
     the waiting (blocking) form (D = 0), and is predicted to read right
     in every trial.

  The program compiles WITH debug (pnut-ts -d) and confines the debugger
  to cog 0 (DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001).  The measuring cog has no debug
  interrupt, no debug() and no BRK, and sets up no interrupt.  Cog 0 only
  polls the mailbox while the measuring cog runs, and each cog has its own
  hub slot.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  No pins, no jumpers, no instruments.  Cog 0
  (Spin2) fills the hub data, sends one command per run, waits for the
  measuring cog (1 s timeout), classifies the records from hub RAM and
  prints them.  The measuring cog (COGINIT, cog execution, PASM below)
  runs every trial from cog RAM, so no instruction fetch from hub comes
  between the instructions under test.
  After the records of every command, the measuring cog writes back the
  RDFAST D value it actually held (MB_ECHO); cog 0 prints RIG FAIL and
  ends the run if it is not the mode sent, so a T run that ran as the
  waiting form cannot print an unearned REFUTED.

HUB LAYOUT (fixed addresses, all below the last 16 KB at $7_C000, which
  holds the debugger and can be write-protected; the program image, its
  VAR space and cog 0's stack sit far below $4_0000 - main() checks the
  stack address at run time and prints RIG FAIL if it is not at least
  16 KB below $4_0000)
    $4_0000  stream source, 64 longs, long k = $1E1E_0000 + k (never
             expected in a record: a record holding one is class F)
    $4_1000  image R: 8 sentinel longs, slot bits 0..7
    $4_2000  image W: 8 write targets, slot bits 0..7
    $4_3000  primer long $A5A5_0001, slot bits 0
    $4_4000  image R / W records (image W: 2,048 longs = 8 KB, to $4_5FFF)
    $4_6000  E7 new[k] = $A5A5_0080 + k (48 longs)   blocking RDFAST's data
    $4_6100  E7 old[k] = $0D0D_0040 + k (48 longs)   prime; old[0] = sync long
    $4_6200  E7 mid[k] = $3C3C_00C0 + k (48 longs)   first RDFAST's data
    $4_7000  E7 records, 18 x 16 x 4 longs, to $4_81FF
  Every region starts on a 32-byte boundary, so long k of a region has
  slot bits k mod 8.  Cog 0 fills the record area with $EEEE_EEEE before
  every command, so a record the measuring cog never wrote is class U.

ONE IMAGE R / W TRIAL (measuring cog, cog execution)
  image R:  dst := seed $C3C3_0003
            rdlong tmp, primer          the last slow read is now $A5A5_0001
            rdfast mode, stream+4*af    the stream under test
            k x nop                     k = 0..8, one hand-written copy each
            rdlong dst, table+4*ar      the RDLONG under test
            100 x djnz (>= 200 clocks), then record dst
  image W:  wrlong old, target+4*aw ; settle ; rb1 := rb2 := seed
            rdlong tmp, primer
            rdfast mode, stream+4*af
            wrlong new, target          the WRLONG under test
            rdlong rb1, target          immediate read-back (T4: a nop)
            settle ; rdlong rb2, target ; record rb1, rb2
  Nothing between the primer and the test instruction other than the
  RDFAST and the k NOPs; no ## operand there (it would add an AUGS).
  Repetition r, cell (af, ar): record (r*8 + af)*8 + ar.  16 repetitions
  of all 64 cells per run.  delta = (ar - af) mod 8 (image W: aw - af).

RECORD CLASSES
  image R record:  P primer   S sentinel   D seed (never written)
  image W cell (rb1 rb2), each:  O old $0F0F_0004   N new $F0F0_0005
                   P primer   D seed
  both images:     F a stream long ($1E1E_0000 + n: data at a RDFAST
                     address), reported by name
                   U $EEEE_EEEE: the measuring cog never wrote the record
                   X other: anything else
  THE "OTHER" SPLIT.  U in any run is RIG FAIL.  X in a control run (C1,
  PS, C2 at any k, C3, C4) is RIG FAIL.  X or F confined to the T runs,
  with every control clean and every cell's repetitions agreeing, is a
  result, not a rig fail: in T1/T2 it refutes "the early RDLONG writes
  the previous read's long" (the RDLONG and WINDOW verdicts name the
  value); in T3/T4 it is a pair the prediction does not name.
  agree code per cell: "." = all 16 repetitions identical, else the
  number (hex) of repetitions identical to repetition 0.

RUNS, IN ORDER.  PREDICTIONS AND REFUTING OUTCOMES ARE FIXED HERE AND IN
  THE predTab TABLE (printed before the run starts)
   C1   image R, NOP in place of the RDFAST, k=0          CONTROL
        MUST: sentinel in all 1,024 records, else RIG FAIL.
   PS   image R, no-wait rdfast, then waitx #200 and rflong in place of
        the k NOPs and the test RDLONG                POSITIVE CONTROL
        MUST: the stream's first long, $1E1E_0000 + af, in all 1,024
        records, else RIG FAIL: it shows that the RDFAST under test, with
        the mode register and address the T runs use, really starts a
        stream at that address - without it, an all-sentinel T1 could be
        a dead RDFAST and not a refutation.
   C2   image R, waiting rdfast (D = 0), k = 0..8          WAITING FORM
        PREDICT: sentinel in all 1,024 records at every k.
        A primer, seed or stream-long record = the waiting form fails (a
        result, not a rig fail); an X or U record is RIG FAIL (the split
        above).
   T1   image R, no-wait rdfast (D = $8000_0000), k = 0
        PREDICT per repetition: 43 primer + 21 sentinel; primer cells by
        delta 0..7 = 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2.
   T2   image R, no-wait rdfast, k = 1..8
        PREDICT per repetition, primer cells by delta (predTab):
          k=1 8 8 8 8 7 6 5 4 = 54    k=5 4 x 8 = 32
          k=2 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 6 = 61    k=6 2 x 8 = 16
          k=3 8 x 8           = 64    k=7 0
          k=4 6 x 8           = 48    k=8 0
        so zero from k = 7: 7 non-hub instructions are a sufficient gap.
   C3   image W, NOP in place of the RDFAST                CONTROL
        MUST: (new,new) in all 1,024 cells, else RIG FAIL.
   C4   image W, waiting rdfast                            WAITING FORM
        PREDICT: (new,new) in every cell.
   T3   image W, no-wait rdfast, immediate read-back
        PREDICT per repetition: 43 (old,old) + 21 (primer,new); (old,old)
        cells by delta = 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2.
   T4   image W, no-wait rdfast, read-back replaced by a NOP
        PREDICT: (seed,new) in all 64 cells.
   E7N  prime / sync rdlong old[0] / waitx phase / getct / rdfast
        $8000_0000, mid[0] / [waitx j-1] / rdfast #0, new[s] / rflong WCZ /
        getct; spacing 2 (j=0) and 4..20 clk (j=1..17); 8 slices x 8
        phases x 16 trials                            POSITIVE CONTROL
        MUST reproduce the failure described above: in every one of the
        64 cells exactly one spacing has wrong reads, within 8..15 clk,
        all 16 trials $0000_0000, the blocking RDFAST taking 2 clk.
        Else RIG FAIL.
   E7B  as E7N, the first RDFAST blocking (D = 0)
        PREDICT: new[s] then new[s+1] in all 18,432 trials, and the two
        RDFASTs together take at least 12 clk (the first one waited).

GATES (each failure prints RIG FAIL; the verdicts it gates print NO VERDICT)
  Ending the run at once: hub layout (checked before any data is written),
       done-flag timeout, mode echo differing from the mode sent.
  Image R / W runs: C1 not clean, PS not clean, C3 not clean, any record
       of class U in any run, any record of class X in a control run, any
       cell whose 16 repetitions disagree (global, every run: the slot
       phase was not fixed; then only T1's total over all repetitions,
       printed, can be read against 43 x 16 = 688).
  RDFAST pairs: E7N did not reproduce the failure, or a record was never
       written.

VERDICTS (printed last), each decided in the order listed
  VERDICT E7 RDLONG:  (T1 against C1, C2 k=0)
    NO VERDICT       an image R / W gate failed
    INCONCLUSIVE     C2 k=0 not clean: T1's primer reads are not shown to
                     belong to the no-wait form
    REFUTED          T1 has seed records (the early value is not the
                     previous read's)
    REFUTED          T1 holds an X value (named, with its count) - same
    REFUTED          T1 holds a stream long (named, with its count) - same
    REFUTED          T1 sentinel in every record (no early completion)
    CONFIRMED        T1: 43 primer per repetition, by delta as predicted
    MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS   primer reads present, every one
                     exactly $A5A5_0001, but not 43 / not the delta split
                     (the early completion is shown; the count is refuted)
  VERDICT E7 WINDOW:  (T1 + T2, k = 0..8)
    NO VERDICT / INCONCLUSIVE (C2 not clean at some k) / REFUTED (seed
    records at some k) / REFUTED (X values at some k, the first named) /
    REFUTED (stream longs at some k, the first named) /
    REFUTED (no primer read at any k) / CONFIRMED
    (every k and delta as predTab; zero from k = 7) / MECHANISM PRESENT,
    COUNT DIFFERS (prints the measured window: the smallest k from which
    every larger k reads zero, or "beyond k=8")
  VERDICT E7 WRLONG:  (T3, T4)
    NO VERDICT / INCONCLUSIVE (C4 not clean) /
    REFUTED - writes land after all: any T3 cell (old,new), or any T4
              cell with rb2 old (early WRLONG's write never lands)
    REFUTED - defect absent: T3 (new,new) in all 64 cells
    REFUTED - a pattern the prediction does not name: a T3 cell outside
              (old,old) (primer,new) (new,new) - X and F values land here -
              or a T4 cell not (seed,new), or NO T3 cell (old,old) (T4
              (seed,new) everywhere is also what a defect-free part gives,
              so the erratum needs at least one lost write)
    CONFIRMED: T3 43 (old,old) + 21 (primer,new) by delta as predicted,
              T4 (seed,new) in all 64
    MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS: otherwise (at least one (old,old))
  VERDICT E7 WAITING FORM:  (C2 all k, C4)
    NO VERDICT / REFUTED - the waiting form fails (any C2 record not
    sentinel, any C4 cell not (new,new)) / INCONCLUSIVE (clean, but T1 and
    T3 did not show the defect) / CONFIRMED
  VERDICT E7 BLOCKING FIRST:  (E7B, gated on E7N)
    NO VERDICT (E7N did not reproduce the failure) / REFUTED (any E7B first or
    second read wrong) / INCONCLUSIVE (the two RDFASTs took under 12 clk
    in some trial: the first did not wait) / CONFIRMED

OPCODES (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the
  .lst hub image; object offset = cog address * 4 + $258).  RDFAST is
  1100011 1LI, WRLONG 1100011 0LI, RDLONG 1011000 CZI, NOP $0000_0000.
  Cog registers: c_mode $0FE, c_pf $106, c_pr $107, c_pw $108, c_dst $109,
  c_rb1 $10A, c_tmp $10D, c_prim $0EF, c_newv $0F7; c_r0..c_r3 $0F8..$0FB
  (contiguous); the cog image ends at c_junk $115 (pasm_end $116).
    rdlong c_tmp,c_prim   $FB021AEF  the primer (every copy)
    rdfast c_mode,c_pf    $FC71FD06  L=0 I=0: D = register, so D[31] is
                                     c_mode's value - $8000_0000 no-wait,
                                     0 waiting - same encoding for C2, T
    rdlong c_dst,c_pr     $FB021307  the RDLONG under test
    nop                   $00000000
    wrlong c_newv,c_pw    $FC61EF08  the WRLONG under test
    rdlong c_rb1,c_pw     $FB021508  immediate read-back
    waitx #200            $FD65901F  PS only
    rflong c_dst          $FD621212  PS only
    wrlong c_mode,ptra[MB_ECHO]  $FC65FD06  at cmd_done ($294), after every
                                     record of the command, before the
                                     done write wrlong #0,ptra ($298)
  Adjacency read from the image (object offsets), primer / RDFAST /
  NOPs / test:
    C1  $308 primer, $30C nop, $310 rdlong                  (0 RDFAST)
    k=0 $318 primer, $31C rdfast, $320 rdlong               (0 NOP)
    k=1 $328, $32C rdfast, $330 nop, $334 rdlong            (1 NOP)
    k=2 $33C, $340 rdfast, $344-$348 nop, $34C rdlong       (2 NOP)
    k=3 $354, $358 rdfast, $35C-$364 nop, $368 rdlong       (3 NOP)
    k=4 $370, $374 rdfast, $378-$384 nop, $388 rdlong       (4 NOP)
    k=5 $390, $394 rdfast, $398-$3A8 nop, $3AC rdlong       (5 NOP)
    k=6 $3B4, $3B8 rdfast, $3BC-$3D0 nop, $3D4 rdlong       (6 NOP)
    k=7 $3DC, $3E0 rdfast, $3E4-$3FC nop, $400 rdlong       (7 NOP)
    k=8 $408, $40C rdfast, $410-$42C nop, $430 rdlong       (8 NOP)
    PS  $438 primer, $43C rdfast, $440 waitx #200, $444 rflong
    C3  $4D0 primer, $4D4 nop, $4D8 wrlong, $4DC rdlong rb1
    W1  $4E4 primer, $4E8 rdfast, $4EC wrlong, $4F0 rdlong rb1 (C4, T3)
    W2  $4F8 primer, $4FC rdfast, $500 wrlong, $504 nop        (T4)
  RDFAST-pair arms (E7N, E7B):
    rdfast c_mode,c_hubf  $FC71FCF3  first RDFAST, D from c_mode
    rdfast #0,c_hubn      $FC78010E  L=1 D=#0: BLOCKING
    rflong c_r1 wcz       $FD79F212
    waitx  c_dly          $FD62221F
    j=0: $544 rdfast / $548 rdfast #0 / $54C rflong;  j>=1: $570 rdfast /
    $574 waitx c_dly / $578 rdfast #0 / $57C rflong.
  DEBUG OUTPUT.  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub
  strings and numbers and sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in
  ln_out(); the only other record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The
  listing reports 2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.

HOW TO RUN
  Compile with pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or
  PNut Ctrl-F10).  Runs once; nothing written to flash.  Output: header
  with every prediction, one block per run (rows + totals), the E7N/E7B rows,
  GATES, RESULTS, the five VERDICT lines, then DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

  ' -- image R / W runs --
  NSLOT           = 8                   ' slot bits: address bits [4:2]
  NCELL           = NSLOT * NSLOT       ' (af, ar) cells per repetition
  REPS            = 16                  ' repetitions of every cell per run
  NREC_R          = REPS * NCELL        ' image R records per run (1,024)
  NREC_W          = REPS * NCELL * 2    ' image W records per run (rb1 + rb2: 2,048)
  KMAX            = 8                   ' NOPs between the RDFAST and the test RDLONG: 0..8
  SETTLE_N        = 100                 ' DJNZ count of a settle loop: >= 200 clocks
  STREAM_WAIT     = 200                 ' PS: WAITX between the no-wait RDFAST and its RFLONG

  PRIMV           = $A5A5_0001          ' primer: the last slow read before the RDFAST
  SENTV           = $5A5A_0002          ' sentinel: what the test RDLONG reads when it waits
  SEEDV           = $C3C3_0003          ' seed: destination before the trial ("never written")
  OLDV            = $0F0F_0004          ' image W: the target before the trial
  NEWV            = $F0F0_0005          ' image W: what the WRLONG under test writes
  STRM_V          = $1E1E_0000          ' stream region long k = STRM_V + k
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' record-area fill: nothing written here
  FIFO_NO_WAIT    = $8000_0000          ' RDFAST D: D[31]=1 no-wait, block count 0 (no wrap)
  FIFO_WAIT       = $0000_0000          ' RDFAST D: D[31]=0 waiting form, block count 0

  T3_PRED_OO      = 43                  ' T3 per repetition: (old,old) cells
  T3_PRED_PN      = 21                  ' T3 per repetition: (primer,new) cells
  T1_TOTAL_PRED   = 43 * REPS           ' T1 primer records over all repetitions (688)

  ' -- RDFAST-pair arms E7N / E7B --
  NPHASE          = 8                   ' egg-beater phases: WAITX 0..7 after the sync
  E7_NCELL        = NSLOT * NPHASE      ' slice x phase cells per arm
  E7_NDIST        = 18                  ' spacing indexes j = 0..17 (2, 4..20 clk)
  TRIALS          = 16                  ' identical trials per (arm, slice, phase, j)
  RECW            = 4                   ' longs per E7 trial record
  REGN            = 48                  ' longs per E7 pattern region
  PRIME_WAIT      = 64                  ' WAITX between the prime RDFAST and its RFLONGs
  SETTLE_WAIT     = 64                  ' WAITX after the prime reads: FIFO refills and idles
  PRIME_READS     = 2                   ' RFLONGs after the prime: FIFO next = old[2]
  GETCT_OVH       = 2                   ' GETCT-pair overhead
  INSTR_CLK       = 2                   ' no-wait RDFAST, RFLONG
  WAITX_BASE      = 2                   ' WAITX D costs 2 + D
  E7_GAP_MIN      = 8                   ' the one failing spacing per cell is in 8..15 clk
  E7_GAP_MAX      = 15
  E7_GAP_SPAN     = E7_GAP_MAX - E7_GAP_MIN + 1
  RDF_BLK_MIN     = 10                  ' a blocking RDFAST takes 10..17 clk
  E7B_MIN_EXC     = RDF_BLK_MIN + INSTR_CLK  ' E7B: two RDFASTs, the first blocking, >= 12 clk

  NEW_BASE        = $A5A5_0080          ' new[k] = NEW_BASE + k
  OLD_BASE        = $0D0D_0040          ' old[k] = OLD_BASE + k
  MID_BASE        = $3C3C_00C0          ' mid[k] = MID_BASE + k
  FLAG_Z_BIT      = 1                   ' E7 record flags: bit 0 = C, bit 1 = Z

  EXC_DIGIT_MAX   = 9                   ' exc codes: 1..9 as digits
  EXC_LETTER_BASE = 10                  '  10..35 as A..Z
  EXC_LETTER_MAX  = 35                  '  above 35: "+"

  ' -- fixed hub layout (HUB LAYOUT in the header) --
  HUB_STRM        = $4_0000             ' stream source, slot 0 aligned
  STRM_LONGS      = 64
  HUB_TBL         = $4_1000             ' image R sentinel table
  HUB_WTBL        = $4_2000             ' image W write targets
  HUB_PRIM        = $4_3000             ' primer long
  HUB_RES         = $4_4000             ' image R / W records
  HUB_E7NEW       = $4_6000             ' E7 new[]
  HUB_E7OLD       = $4_6100             ' E7 old[]
  HUB_E7MID       = $4_6200             ' E7 mid[]
  HUB_E7BUF       = $4_7000             ' E7 records
  E7_BUF_LONGS    = E7_NDIST * TRIALS * RECW
  HUB_DATA_LO     = HUB_STRM            ' lowest data byte
  HUB_DATA_END    = HUB_E7BUF + E7_BUF_LONGS * 4   ' first byte above the data ($4_8200)
  HUB_TOP16K      = $7_C000             ' the last 16 KB of hub RAM starts here
  STACK_MARGIN    = $4000               ' room demanded between cog 0's stack and the data

  STAT_READY      = $0000_0A11          ' measuring cog is up
  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars); longer text is cut

  SUCCESS         = 0
  E_RIG_FAIL      = -1                  ' the measuring cog did not answer within 1 s
  E_MODE_FAIL     = -2                  ' the mode echoed back differs from the mode sent

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  ' commands to the measuring cog (MB_CMD)
  #1, CMD_R, CMD_W, CMD_E7

  ' image R / W runs, in run order: C1, PS, C2 k=0..8, T1 (k=0), T2 k=1..8, C3, C4, T3, T4
  RUN_C1          = 0
  RUN_PS          = 1                   ' positive control: the RDFAST under test starts a stream
  RUN_C2          = 2                   ' RUN_C2 + k, k = 0..8
  RUN_T1          = RUN_C2 + KMAX + 1   ' RUN_T1 + k: k = 0 is T1, k = 1..8 is T2
  RUN_C3          = RUN_T1 + KMAX + 1
  RUN_C4          = RUN_C3 + 1
  RUN_T3          = RUN_C4 + 1
  RUN_T4          = RUN_T3 + 1
  NRUN            = RUN_T4 + 1

  ' trial copies in the measuring cog: image R copy k (0..8) has k NOPs; COPY_RNOP = C1;
  ' COPY_RSTRM = PS
  COPY_RNOP       = KMAX + 1
  COPY_RSTRM      = KMAX + 2
  #0, COPY_WNOP, COPY_W1, COPY_W2

  ' value classes (image R uses P S D F U X; image W uses O N P D F U X).
  ' F = a stream long (STRM_V + n: the data at a RDFAST address), U = the
  ' record-area fill (the measuring cog never wrote it), X = anything else.
  #0, VC_OLD, VC_NEW, VC_PRIM, VC_SEED, VC_SENT, VC_STRM, VC_UNWR, VC_OTHER
  NVC             = VC_OTHER + 1
  NPAIR           = NVC * NVC           ' image W cell code = rb1 class * NVC + rb2 class
  PAIR_OO         = VC_OLD * NVC + VC_OLD
  PAIR_ON         = VC_OLD * NVC + VC_NEW
  PAIR_NN         = VC_NEW * NVC + VC_NEW
  PAIR_PN         = VC_PRIM * NVC + VC_NEW
  PAIR_DN         = VC_SEED * NVC + VC_NEW

  ' E7 arms
  #0, AE_N, AE_B
  NAE             = AE_B + 1

  ' E7 read classes
  #0, C_OK, C_STALE, C_OLD, C_MID, C_NEWSH, C_ZERO, C_OTHER
  NCLS            = C_OTHER + 1

  ' mailbox longs (cog 0 <-> measuring cog)
  '  MB_CMD   - 0 idle / CMD_*; the measuring cog writes 0 when done
  '  MB_COPY  - trial copy (image R / W)
  '  MB_MODE  - the RDFAST D value (FIFO_WAIT / FIFO_NO_WAIT)
  '  MB_SLICE, MB_PHASE - E7 cell
  '  MB_ALIVE - STAT_READY once the measuring cog runs
  '  MB_ECHO  - the RDFAST D value the measuring cog actually held, written
  '             back in the command epilogue (after the records)
  #0, MB_CMD, MB_COPY, MB_MODE, MB_SLICE, MB_PHASE, MB_ALIVE, MB_ECHO, MB_LEN

  ' E7 record longs
  #0, REC_EL, REC_V1, REC_V2, REC_FLAGS

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  ' image R / W runs, per run
  byte cellCode[NRUN * NCELL]           ' repetition 0: value class (R) or pair code (W)
  byte cellAgree[NRUN * NCELL]          ' repetitions identical to repetition 0
  long runCnt[NRUN * NVC]               ' value classes over all repetitions (W: rb1 and rb2)
  long runRep0[NRUN * NPAIR]            ' repetition-0 cells per code
  long runDelta[NRUN * NSLOT]           ' repetition 0 by delta: R primer cells, W (old,old) cells
  long runDisagree[NRUN]                ' cells whose 16 repetitions are not identical
  long runGoodAll[NRUN]                 ' over all repetitions: R sentinel records, W (new,new) cells
  long runOther[NRUN]                   ' values classified X
  long runOtherVal[NRUN]                ' the first X value
  long runStrmVal[NRUN]                 ' the first F (stream long) value
  long runDamage                        ' data longs changed during the image R / W runs
  ' RDFAST-pair arms
  long e7BadGaps[NAE * E7_NCELL]        ' spacings with a wrong trial, per cell
  long e7BadJ[NAE * E7_NCELL]           ' the last such spacing index
  long e7Pure[NAE * E7_NCELL]           ' that spacing: 16/16 zero, blocking RDFAST 2 clk
  long e7Tot[NAE], e7Good[NAE], e7V2Bad[NAE], e7ExcMin[NAE], e7ExcMax[NAE]
  long e7Cls[NAE * NCLS]
  long e7BadSlice[NAE], e7BadPhase[NAE], e7BadDist[NAE], e7BadGot[NAE]
  long e7Unwritten, e7Damage
  long gapHist[E7_GAP_SPAN]
  ' print buffers
  byte rowStr[NSLOT * 3 + 1]
  byte agreeStr[NSLOT + 1]
  byte clsRow[E7_NDIST + 1]
  byte excRow[E7_NDIST + 1]
  ' every printed line is built here and sent by ONE debug() record (ln_out)
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | runIdx, armE, sliceIdx, phaseIdx, cog, startCt, status, pStack, damageCnt, bRunsOk, bReproduced
'' Run every image R / W run and both RDFAST-pair arms on the measuring
'' cog, print the raw rows, then the gates and the verdicts.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - image R / W run id (RUN_*)
' @local armE - E7 arm (AE_*)
' @local sliceIdx - E7: hub slice of the blocking RDFAST's address
' @local phaseIdx - E7: egg-beater phase (WAITX after the sync)
' @local cog - cog the measuring cog started in
' @local startCt - CT at the start of the start-up timeout
' @local status - SUCCESS, or E_RIG_FAIL
' @local pStack - hub address of this method's locals: cog 0's stack
' @local damageCnt - data longs changed by the command just run
' @local bRunsOk - every image R / W gate passed
' @local bReproduced - E7N reproduced E7

  pStack := @status
  linePos := 0
  ' the layout check runs before the first write to the fixed data area it protects
  if pStack + STACK_MARGIN > HUB_DATA_LO or HUB_DATA_END > HUB_TOP16K
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: hub layout - cog 0 stack at "))
    ln_h(pStack)
    ln_s(string(" must lie at least "))
    ln_h(STACK_MARGIN)
    ln_s(string(" below the data at "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_LO)
    ln_s(string(", and the data end "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
    ln_s(string(" must lie below "))
    ln_h(HUB_TOP16K)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  reset_tallies()
  fill_regions()
  mbox[MB_CMD] := 0
  mbox[MB_ALIVE] := 0

  print_header(pStack)

  cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if cog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(cog)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_ALIVE] == STAT_READY
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog start-up expected $0000_0A11 within 1 s, got "))
      ln_h(mbox[MB_ALIVE])
      ln_out()
      finish()
  ln_s(string("measuring cog "))
  ln_d(cog)
  say(string(" running"))

  ' ---- image R / W runs ------------------------------------------------------------
  repeat runIdx from 0 to NRUN - 1
    print_run_header(runIdx)
    longfill(HUB_RES, UNWRITTEN, NREC_W)
    if run_is_r(runIdx)
      status := send_cmd(CMD_R, run_copy(runIdx), run_mode(runIdx), 0, 0)
    else
      status := send_cmd(CMD_W, run_copy(runIdx), run_mode(runIdx), 0, 0)
    if status == E_RIG_FAIL
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not finish run "))
      ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
      ln_s(string(" k"))
      ln_d(run_k(runIdx))
      say(string(" within 1 s (done flag never cleared)"))
    if status <> SUCCESS
      finish()
    if runIdx == RUN_PS
      process_ps()
    elseif run_is_r(runIdx)
      process_r(runIdx)
    else
      process_w(runIdx)
    print_run(runIdx)
    damageCnt := region_damage()
    if damageCnt > 0
      runDamage += damageCnt
      ln_s(string("  REGION DAMAGE after "))
      ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
      ln_s(string(" k"))
      ln_d(run_k(runIdx))
      ln_s(string(": "))
      ln_d(damageCnt)
      say(string(" data longs changed (a stray hub write) - regions re-filled"))
      fill_regions()

  ' ---- E7 arms -------------------------------------------------------------
  repeat armE from AE_N to AE_B
    print_e7_header(armE)
    repeat sliceIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
      repeat phaseIdx from 0 to NPHASE - 1
        longfill(HUB_E7BUF, UNWRITTEN, E7_BUF_LONGS)
        status := send_cmd(CMD_E7, 0, e7_mode(armE), sliceIdx, phaseIdx)
        if status == E_RIG_FAIL
          ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not finish "))
          ln_s(e7_name(armE))
          ln_s(string(" slice "))
          ln_d(sliceIdx)
          ln_s(string(" phase "))
          ln_d(phaseIdx)
          say(string(" within 1 s"))
        if status <> SUCCESS
          finish()
        process_e7(armE, sliceIdx, phaseIdx)
        damageCnt := region_damage()
        if damageCnt > 0
          e7Damage += damageCnt
          ln_s(string("  REGION DAMAGE after "))
          ln_s(e7_name(armE))
          ln_s(string(" s"))
          ln_d(sliceIdx)
          ln_s(string(" p"))
          ln_d(phaseIdx)
          ln_s(string(": "))
          ln_d(damageCnt)
          say(string(" data longs changed - regions re-filled"))
          fill_regions()

  ' ---- gates ---------------------------------------------------------------
  say(string("=== GATES ==="))
  bRunsOk := runs_gate()
  bReproduced := e7_gate()

  ' ---- results -------------------------------------------------------------
  say(string("=== RESULTS ==="))
  print_window_table()
  verdict_rdlong(bRunsOk)
  verdict_window(bRunsOk)
  verdict_wrlong(bRunsOk)
  verdict_waiting(bRunsOk)
  verdict_e7b(bReproduced)

  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_d(value) | divisor, bStarted
' Append a signed decimal (the form udec_/sdec_ printed) to the line.
'
' @param value - the value

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  if value == NEGX
    ln_s(string("-2147483648"))
  else
    if value < 0
      ln_c("-")
      value := -value
    divisor := 1_000_000_000
    bStarted := FALSE
    repeat 10
      if value >= divisor or bStarted or divisor == 1
        ln_c("0" + value / divisor)
        value //= divisor
        bStarted := TRUE
      divisor /= 10

PRI ln_h(value) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as uhex_long_ printed it: $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param value - the value

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from 7 to 0
    nibble := (value >> (idx * 4)) & $F
    if nibble < 10
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - 10)
    if idx == 4
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_row8(pLongs) | idx
' Append 8 longs as decimals separated by single spaces.
'
' @param pLongs - hub address of the first long

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index 0..7

  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if idx > 0
      ln_c(" ")
    ln_d(long[pLongs][idx])

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' set-up and the command channel
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header(pStack) | kIdx
' Print the rig identity, the hub layout and every prediction before the run.
'
' @param pStack - hub address of main()'s locals (cog 0's stack)

' Local Variables:
' @local kIdx - NOP count k

  say(string("=== P2 Errata, Erratum E7: next hub instruction after a no-wait RDFAST; + blocking-first arm (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz) ==="))
  say(string("values: primer $A5A5_0001  sentinel $5A5A_0002  seed $C3C3_0003  old $0F0F_0004  new $F0F0_0005  stream long k $1E1E_0000+k  unwritten $EEEE_EEEE"))
  ln_s(string("hub: stream "))
  ln_h(HUB_STRM)
  ln_s(string(" table "))
  ln_h(HUB_TBL)
  ln_s(string(" targets "))
  ln_h(HUB_WTBL)
  ln_s(string(" primer "))
  ln_h(HUB_PRIM)
  ln_s(string(" records "))
  ln_h(HUB_RES)
  ln_s(string(" E7 new/old/mid "))
  ln_h(HUB_E7NEW)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_E7OLD)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_E7MID)
  ln_s(string(" E7 records "))
  ln_h(HUB_E7BUF)
  ln_s(string("; data end "))
  ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
  ln_s(string("; measuring-cog image "))
  ln_h(@pasm)
  ln_s(string("; last VAR byte array "))
  ln_h(@lineBuf)
  ln_s(string("; cog 0 stack "))
  ln_h(pStack)
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("record codes: image R  P primer  S sentinel  D seed (never written)  F stream long  U unwritten  X other | image W cell rb1 rb2 each  O old  N new  P primer  D seed  F  U  X | "))
  say(string("agree: . all 16 identical, else hex count identical to rep 0"))
  say(string("delta = (ar - af) mod 8 (image W: aw - af). Every run: 16 repetitions x 64 cells. Predicted primer cells per repetition (T1 k=0, T2 k=1..8), by delta 0..7:"))
  repeat kIdx from 0 to KMAX
    ln_s(string("  predicted k="))
    ln_d(kIdx)
    ln_s(string(": "))
    ln_row8(@predTab + kIdx * NSLOT * 4)
    ln_s(string(" = "))
    ln_d(predTot[kIdx])
    say(string(" of 64"))
  ln_s(string("predicted T3 per repetition: "))
  ln_d(T3_PRED_OO)
  ln_s(string(" (old,old) by delta as k=0 above + "))
  ln_d(T3_PRED_PN)
  say(string(" (primer,new); T4: (seed,new) in all 64; C1, C2, C4: clean; C3: (new,new)"))
  say(string("refuting outcomes (reads): T1 sentinel everywhere (no early completion); seed, a stream long or any other value in a T1/T2 record (value not the previous read's); C2/C4 not clean (waiting form fails)"))
  say(string("refuting outcomes (writes): T3 (new,new) everywhere (absent); T3 (old,new) or T4 rb2 old (writes land after all); T3 with no (old,old) cell, or any unnamed pair (pattern not predicted)"))
  say(string("rig fails: U (unwritten) in any run; X (other) in a control run C1 PS C2 C3 C4; C1/PS/C3 not clean; any cell's repetitions disagree; the mode the measuring cog echoes back differs from the mode sent"))
  say(string("E7: E7N must show E7 (one failing spacing per cell, 8..15 clk, 16/16 $0000_0000, blocking RDFAST 2 clk); E7B predicted: every read right. spacing j: 0 = 2 clk, j>=1 = waitx j-1 = j+3 clk"))

PRI fill_regions() | idx
' Write every fixed data region its pattern.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    long[HUB_STRM][idx] := STRM_V + idx
  longfill(HUB_TBL, SENTV, NSLOT)
  longfill(HUB_WTBL, OLDV, NSLOT)
  long[HUB_PRIM] := PRIMV
  repeat idx from 0 to REGN - 1
    long[HUB_E7NEW][idx] := patnew(idx)
    long[HUB_E7OLD][idx] := patold(idx)
    long[HUB_E7MID][idx] := patmid(idx)

PRI region_damage() : damageCnt | idx
' Count read-only data longs that no longer hold their pattern.
'
' @returns damageCnt - changed longs (stream, table, primer, E7 regions)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  damageCnt := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    if long[HUB_STRM][idx] <> STRM_V + idx
      damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if long[HUB_TBL][idx] <> SENTV
      damageCnt++
  if long[HUB_PRIM] <> PRIMV
    damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to REGN - 1
    if long[HUB_E7NEW][idx] <> patnew(idx)
      damageCnt++
    if long[HUB_E7OLD][idx] <> patold(idx)
      damageCnt++
    if long[HUB_E7MID][idx] <> patmid(idx)
      damageCnt++

PRI reset_tallies()
' Clear every tally.
'

  bytefill(@cellCode, 0, NRUN * NCELL)
  bytefill(@cellAgree, 0, NRUN * NCELL)
  longfill(@runCnt, 0, NRUN * NVC)
  longfill(@runRep0, 0, NRUN * NPAIR)
  longfill(@runDelta, 0, NRUN * NSLOT)
  longfill(@runDisagree, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runGoodAll, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOther, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOtherVal, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runStrmVal, 0, NRUN)
  runDamage := 0
  longfill(@e7BadGaps, 0, NAE * E7_NCELL)
  longfill(@e7BadJ, -1, NAE * E7_NCELL)
  longfill(@e7Pure, FALSE, NAE * E7_NCELL)
  longfill(@e7Tot, 0, NAE)
  longfill(@e7Good, 0, NAE)
  longfill(@e7V2Bad, 0, NAE)
  longfill(@e7ExcMin, POSX, NAE)
  longfill(@e7ExcMax, NEGX, NAE)
  longfill(@e7Cls, 0, NAE * NCLS)
  longfill(@e7BadDist, -1, NAE)
  e7Unwritten := 0
  e7Damage := 0
  longfill(@gapHist, 0, E7_GAP_SPAN)

PRI send_cmd(cmdId, copyIdx, modeVal, sliceIdx, phaseIdx) : status | startCt
' Hand one command to the measuring cog and wait for it to clear MB_CMD.
'
' @param cmdId - CMD_R / CMD_W / CMD_E7
' @param copyIdx - trial copy (image R: k or COPY_RNOP; image W: COPY_W*)
' @param modeVal - the RDFAST D value under test
' @param sliceIdx - hub slice of the blocking RDFAST's address
' @param phaseIdx - egg-beater phase
' @returns status - SUCCESS; E_RIG_FAIL on a 1 s timeout; E_MODE_FAIL (after
'   printing its RIG FAIL line) when the mode the measuring cog echoed back is
'   not the mode sent

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the command was issued

  status := SUCCESS
  mbox[MB_COPY] := copyIdx
  mbox[MB_MODE] := modeVal
  mbox[MB_SLICE] := sliceIdx
  mbox[MB_PHASE] := phaseIdx
  mbox[MB_ECHO] := UNWRITTEN
  mbox[MB_CMD] := cmdId
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_CMD] == 0
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      status := E_RIG_FAIL
      quit
  if status == SUCCESS and mbox[MB_ECHO] <> modeVal
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: command "))
    ln_d(cmdId)
    ln_s(string(" copy "))
    ln_d(copyIdx)
    ln_s(string(" slice "))
    ln_d(sliceIdx)
    ln_s(string(" phase "))
    ln_d(phaseIdx)
    ln_s(string(" ran with RDFAST D "))
    ln_h(mbox[MB_ECHO])
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(modeVal)
    say(string(" (mode echo)"))
    status := E_MODE_FAIL

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' image R / W run tables
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI run_is_r(runIdx) : bImageR
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bImageR - TRUE for an image R (RDLONG) run

  bImageR := runIdx < RUN_C3

PRI run_k(runIdx) : kVal
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns kVal - NOPs between the RDFAST and the test instruction

  if runIdx >= RUN_C2 and runIdx < RUN_T1
    kVal := runIdx - RUN_C2
  elseif runIdx >= RUN_T1 and runIdx < RUN_C3
    kVal := runIdx - RUN_T1
  else
    kVal := 0

PRI run_copy(runIdx) : copyIdx
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns copyIdx - the measuring cog's trial copy for the run

  if runIdx == RUN_C1
    copyIdx := COPY_RNOP
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PS
    copyIdx := COPY_RSTRM
  elseif run_is_r(runIdx)
    copyIdx := run_k(runIdx)
  else
    copyIdx := lookupz(runIdx - RUN_C3: COPY_WNOP, COPY_W1, COPY_W1, COPY_W2)

PRI run_mode(runIdx) : modeVal
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns modeVal - the RDFAST D value (unused by the NOP copies C1, C3)

  if (runIdx >= RUN_T1 and runIdx < RUN_C3) or runIdx == RUN_PS or runIdx == RUN_T3 or runIdx == RUN_T4
    modeVal := FIFO_NO_WAIT
  else
    modeVal := FIFO_WAIT

PRI run_name(runIdx) : pName
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns pName - printable run name

  if runIdx == RUN_C1
    pName := string("C1")
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PS
    pName := string("PS")
  elseif runIdx < RUN_T1
    pName := string("C2")
  elseif runIdx == RUN_T1
    pName := string("T1")
  elseif runIdx < RUN_C3
    pName := string("T2")
  else
    pName := lookupz(runIdx - RUN_C3: string("C3"), string("C4"), string("T3"), string("T4"))

PRI pred(kIdx, deltaIdx) : cnt
' @param kIdx - NOP count k
' @param deltaIdx - delta 0..7
' @returns cnt - predicted primer cells per repetition (predTab)

  cnt := predTab[kIdx * NSLOT + deltaIdx]

PRI cell_delta(cellIdx) : deltaIdx
' @param cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @returns deltaIdx - (ar - af) mod 8

  deltaIdx := ((cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1)) - (cellIdx >> 3)) & (NSLOT - 1)

PRI class_r(datum) : cls
' @param datum - the value to classify
' @returns cls - VC_PRIM / VC_SENT / VC_SEED / VC_UNWR / VC_STRM / VC_OTHER

  if datum == PRIMV
    cls := VC_PRIM
  elseif datum == SENTV
    cls := VC_SENT
  elseif datum == SEEDV
    cls := VC_SEED
  else
    cls := class_rest(datum)

PRI class_rest(datum) : cls
' The classes shared by both images after their own values: never written,
' a stream long, or anything else.
'
' @param datum - the value to classify
' @returns cls - VC_UNWR / VC_STRM / VC_OTHER

  if datum == UNWRITTEN
    cls := VC_UNWR
  elseif (datum - STRM_V) +< STRM_LONGS
    cls := VC_STRM
  else
    cls := VC_OTHER

PRI class_w(datum) : cls
' @param datum - the value to classify
' @returns cls - VC_OLD / VC_NEW / VC_PRIM / VC_SEED / VC_UNWR / VC_STRM / VC_OTHER

  if datum == OLDV
    cls := VC_OLD
  elseif datum == NEWV
    cls := VC_NEW
  elseif datum == PRIMV
    cls := VC_PRIM
  elseif datum == SEEDV
    cls := VC_SEED
  else
    cls := class_rest(datum)

PRI vcchar(cls) : codeChar
' @param cls - the class code
' @returns codeChar - O N P D S F U X

  codeChar := lookupz(cls: "O", "N", "P", "D", "S", "F", "U", "X")

PRI agreechar(agreeCnt) : codeChar
' @param agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0 (1..16)
' @returns codeChar - "." for all 16, else the hex digit

  if agreeCnt == REPS
    codeChar := "."
  elseif agreeCnt < 10
    codeChar := "0" + agreeCnt
  else
    codeChar := "A" + agreeCnt - 10

PRI note_value(runIdx, cls, datum)
' Count one classified value; keep the run's first X and first F values.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @param cls - the class code
' @param datum - the value to classify

  if cls == VC_STRM and runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_STRM] == 0
    runStrmVal[runIdx] := datum
  runCnt[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
  if cls == VC_OTHER
    if runOther[runIdx] == 0
      runOtherVal[runIdx] := datum
    runOther[runIdx]++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' image R / W: classify and print one run
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI process_r(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, datum, cls, agreeCnt
' Classify an image R run: repetition-0 codes, agreement, totals, delta split.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's record
' @local datum - a record
' @local cls - its class
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][cellIdx]
    cls := class_r(firstVal)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + cls]++
    if cls == VC_PRIM
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      datum := long[HUB_RES][repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]
      note_value(runIdx, class_r(datum), datum)
      if datum == SENTV
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if datum == firstVal
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI process_ps() | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, datum, agreeCnt, expVal
' Classify the PS run: every record must be the stream's first long, STRM_V + af.
' Cell code 1 = right, 0 = wrong; wrong values count against PS only (not as X).
'

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's record
' @local datum - a record
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local expVal - the stream's first long for this af

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    expVal := STRM_V + (cellIdx >> 3)
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][cellIdx]
    if firstVal == expVal
      cellCode[RUN_PS * NCELL + cellIdx] := 1
    else
      cellCode[RUN_PS * NCELL + cellIdx] := 0
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      datum := long[HUB_RES][repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]
      if datum == expVal
        runGoodAll[RUN_PS]++
      elseif runOtherVal[RUN_PS] == 0
        runOtherVal[RUN_PS] := datum
      if datum == UNWRITTEN
        runCnt[RUN_PS * NVC + VC_UNWR]++
      if datum == firstVal
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[RUN_PS * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[RUN_PS]++

PRI process_w(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstRb1, firstRb2, rb1, rb2, pairCode, agreeCnt, recIdx
' Classify an image W run: repetition-0 pair codes, agreement, totals, delta split.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + aw
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstRb1 - repetition 0's rb1
' @local firstRb2 - repetition 0's rb2
' @local rb1 - immediate read-back
' @local rb2 - settled read-back
' @local pairCode - class(rb1) * NVC + class(rb2)
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local recIdx - trial index (record pair 2*recIdx, 2*recIdx+1)

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstRb1 := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx]
    firstRb2 := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx + 1]
    pairCode := class_w(firstRb1) * NVC + class_w(firstRb2)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := pairCode
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + pairCode]++
    if pairCode == PAIR_OO
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      recIdx := repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx
      rb1 := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx]
      rb2 := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx + 1]
      note_value(runIdx, class_w(rb1), rb1)
      note_value(runIdx, class_w(rb2), rb2)
      if rb1 == NEWV and rb2 == NEWV
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if rb1 == firstRb1 and rb2 == firstRb2
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI print_run_header(runIdx) | kVal
' Print the run's sequence, its prediction and what refutes it, before its rows.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

' Local Variables:
' @local kVal - NOPs in the run's copy

  kVal := run_k(runIdx)
  if runIdx == RUN_C1
    say(string("RUN C1 (CONTROL, image R): rdlong primer / NOP in place of the RDFAST / rdlong test. MUST: sentinel in all 1024 records, else RIG FAIL"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_PS
    ln_s(string("RUN PS (POSITIVE CONTROL, image R): rdlong primer / rdfast D=$8000_0000 / waitx #200 / rflong. MUST: the stream's first long $1E1E_0000+af in all 1024 records, "))
    say(string("else RIG FAIL (the RDFAST under test would not be starting a stream)"))
  elseif runIdx < RUN_T1
    ln_s(string("RUN C2 k="))
    ln_d(kVal)
    ln_s(string(" (WAITING FORM, image R): rdlong primer / rdfast D=0 / "))
    ln_d(kVal)
    say(string(" NOP / rdlong test. PREDICT: sentinel in all 1024 records; any other = the waiting form fails"))
  elseif runIdx < RUN_C3
    ln_s(string("RUN "))
    ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
    ln_s(string(" k="))
    ln_d(kVal)
    ln_s(string(" (image R): rdlong primer / rdfast D=$8000_0000 / "))
    ln_d(kVal)
    ln_s(string(" NOP / rdlong test. PREDICT per repetition: "))
    ln_d(predTot[kVal])
    ln_s(string(" primer, by delta "))
    ln_row8(@predTab + kVal * NSLOT * 4)
    say(string("; every other record sentinel"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_C3
    say(string("RUN C3 (CONTROL, image W): rdlong primer / NOP in place of the RDFAST / wrlong new / rdlong rb1 ... rdlong rb2. MUST: (new,new) in all 1024 cells, else RIG FAIL"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_C4
    say(string("RUN C4 (WAITING FORM, image W): rdlong primer / rdfast D=0 / wrlong new / rdlong rb1 ... rdlong rb2. PREDICT: (new,new) in every cell; any other = the waiting form fails"))
  elseif runIdx == RUN_T3
    ln_s(string("RUN T3 (image W, W1): rdlong primer / rdfast D=$8000_0000 / wrlong new / rdlong rb1 ... rdlong rb2. "))
    say(string("PREDICT per repetition: 43 (old,old) by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 + 21 (primer,new). (old,new) = write late not lost: REFUTED"))
  else
    say(string("RUN T4 (image W, W2): rdlong primer / rdfast D=$8000_0000 / wrlong new / NOP ... rdlong rb2. PREDICT: (seed,new) in all 64 cells. rb2 old = the early WRLONG's write never lands: REFUTED"))

PRI ln_runk(runIdx)
' Append "  <run name> k<k>", the lead of every per-run row.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
  ln_s(string(" k"))
  ln_d(run_k(runIdx))

PRI print_run(runIdx) | afIdx, arIdx, cellIdx, pairCode, base, kVal
' Print a run's raw rows (repetition 0 per af, agreement) and its totals.
'
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)

' Local Variables:
' @local afIdx - stream slot bits
' @local arIdx - test-address slot bits
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local pairCode - image W cell code
' @local base - index of the run's first count
' @local kVal - NOPs in the run's copy

  kVal := run_k(runIdx)
  repeat afIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    repeat arIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
      cellIdx := runIdx * NCELL + afIdx * NSLOT + arIdx
      agreeStr[arIdx] := agreechar(cellAgree[cellIdx])
      if runIdx == RUN_PS
        rowStr[arIdx] := lookupz(cellCode[cellIdx]: "X", ".")
      elseif run_is_r(runIdx)
        rowStr[arIdx] := vcchar(cellCode[cellIdx])
      else
        pairCode := cellCode[cellIdx]
        rowStr[arIdx * 3] := vcchar(pairCode / NVC)
        rowStr[arIdx * 3 + 1] := vcchar(pairCode // NVC)
        rowStr[arIdx * 3 + 2] := " "
    agreeStr[NSLOT] := 0
    if run_is_r(runIdx)
      rowStr[NSLOT] := 0
    else
      rowStr[NSLOT * 3 - 1] := 0
    ln_runk(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" af"))
    ln_d(afIdx)
    ln_s(string(" rep0 a0-7: "))
    ln_s(@rowStr)
    ln_s(string("  agree "))
    say(@agreeStr)
  base := runIdx * NVC
  if runIdx == RUN_PS
    ln_s(string("  PS all reps: stream's first long right in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_PS])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R)
    ln_s(string(" records (. right, X wrong); first wrong value "))
    ln_h(runOtherVal[RUN_PS])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[RUN_PS])
    ln_out()
  elseif run_is_r(runIdx)
    ln_runk(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" sentinel "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SENT])
    ln_s(string(" seed "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R)
    ln_s(string(" | rep0 primer "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  else
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
    ln_s(string(" all reps, values (rb1+rb2): old "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OLD])
    ln_s(string(" new "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_NEW])
    ln_s(string(" primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" seed "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_W)
    ln_s(string("; (new,new) cells "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R)
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_s(run_name(runIdx))
    ln_s(string(" rep0 cells: OO "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_OO])
    ln_s(string(" PN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_PN])
    ln_s(string(" NN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_NN])
    ln_s(string(" ON "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_ON])
    ln_s(string(" DN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_DN])
    ln_s(string(" any other pair "))
    ln_d(NCELL - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_OO] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_PN] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_NN] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_ON] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_DN])
    ln_s(string(" | OO by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_out()
  if runOther[runIdx] > 0
    ln_runk(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" first other value "))
    ln_h(runOtherVal[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" ("))
    ln_d(runOther[runIdx])
    say(string(" other values in the run)"))
  if runCnt[base + VC_STRM] > 0
    ln_runk(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" stream longs (F, data at a RDFAST address): "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" values, first "))
    ln_h(runStrmVal[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  if runCnt[base + VC_UNWR] > 0
    ln_runk(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" never written (U, $EEEE_EEEE): "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_UNWR])
    say(string(" records"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' E7 arms
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI e7_name(armE) : pName
' @param armE - E7 arm (AE_*)
' @returns pName - printable arm name

  pName := lookupz(armE: string("E7N"), string("E7B"))

PRI e7_mode(armE) : modeVal
' @param armE - E7 arm (AE_*)
' @returns modeVal - D of the first RDFAST

  modeVal := lookupz(armE: FIFO_NO_WAIT, FIFO_WAIT)

PRI waitx_clk(distIdx) : clks
' @param distIdx - spacing index j
' @returns clks - clocks of the WAITX between the two RDFASTs (0 at j = 0)

  if distIdx == 0
    clks := 0
  else
    clks := WAITX_BASE + distIdx - 1

PRI distclk(distIdx) : clks
' Spacing, issue to issue, from a no-wait first RDFAST to the blocking one (E7N).
'
' @param distIdx - spacing index j
' @returns clks - 2 at j = 0, else j + 3

  clks := INSTR_CLK + waitx_clk(distIdx)

PRI e7base(armE, distIdx) : baseClk
' The elapsed GETCT count with exc = 0.  E7N: exc = the blocking RDFAST's
' clocks.  E7B: exc = the two RDFASTs' clocks together.
'
' @param armE - E7 arm (AE_*)
' @param distIdx - spacing index j
' @returns baseClk - no-stall elapsed clocks

  if armE == AE_N
    baseClk := GETCT_OVH + distclk(distIdx) + INSTR_CLK
  else
    baseClk := GETCT_OVH + waitx_clk(distIdx) + INSTR_CLK

PRI patnew(longIdx) : pattern
' @param longIdx - long index
' @returns pattern - new[longIdx]

  pattern := NEW_BASE + longIdx

PRI patold(longIdx) : pattern
' @param longIdx - long index
' @returns pattern - old[longIdx]

  pattern := OLD_BASE + longIdx

PRI patmid(longIdx) : pattern
' @param longIdx - long index
' @returns pattern - mid[longIdx]

  pattern := MID_BASE + longIdx

PRI e7class(sliceIdx, datum) : cls
' @param sliceIdx - hub slice of the blocking RDFAST's address
' @param datum - the value to classify
' @returns cls - C_*

  if datum == patnew(sliceIdx)
    cls := C_OK
  elseif datum == patold(PRIME_READS)
    cls := C_STALE
  elseif (datum - OLD_BASE) +< REGN
    cls := C_OLD
  elseif (datum - MID_BASE) +< REGN
    cls := C_MID
  elseif (datum - NEW_BASE) +< REGN
    cls := C_NEWSH
  elseif datum == 0
    cls := C_ZERO
  else
    cls := C_OTHER

PRI clschar(cls) : codeChar
' @param cls - the class code
' @returns codeChar - . S o M N Z X

  codeChar := lookupz(cls: ".", "S", "o", "M", "N", "Z", "X")

PRI excchar(excess) : codeChar
' @param excess - elapsed minus the no-stall count
' @returns codeChar - . 1-9 A-Z + -

  if excess == 0
    codeChar := "."
  elseif excess < 0
    codeChar := "-"
  elseif excess <= EXC_DIGIT_MAX
    codeChar := "0" + excess
  elseif excess <= EXC_LETTER_MAX
    codeChar := "A" + excess - EXC_LETTER_BASE
  else
    codeChar := "+"

PRI print_e7_header(armE)
' @param armE - E7 arm (AE_*)

  if armE == AE_N
    say(string("ARM E7N (POSITIVE CONTROL, Erratum E7 failure): rdlong old[0] / waitx phase / getct / rdfast $8000_0000,mid[0] / [waitx j-1] / rdfast #0,new[s] / rflong WCZ / getct / rflong"))
    ln_s(string("  MUST: per cell exactly one spacing in 8..15 clk wrong, 16/16 $0000_0000, blocking RDFAST 2 clk (exc); spacings 2, 4..7, 16..20 right. Else RIG FAIL. "))
    say(string("cls . ok S stale old[2] o old M mid N new wrong long Z zero X other * disagree"))
  else
    say(string("ARM E7B (FIRST RDFAST BLOCKING): as E7N with rdfast D=0 first. exc = both RDFASTs' clocks. PREDICT: new[s] then new[s+1] in every trial (V = first right, second wrong); exc >= 12"))

PRI process_e7(armE, sliceIdx, phaseIdx) | distIdx, trialIdx, pRec, cls, bOk, goodCnt, zeroCnt, v2Cnt, excess, firstExc, bExcMixed, firstChar, codeChar, bMixed, cellIdx, baseClk, pShow
' Classify, tally and print one (arm, slice, phase) cell of E7 records.
'
' @param armE - E7 arm (AE_*)
' @param sliceIdx - hub slice of the blocking RDFAST's address
' @param phaseIdx - egg-beater phase

' Local Variables:
' @local distIdx - spacing index j
' @local trialIdx - trial
' @local pRec - hub address of the trial record
' @local cls - class of the first read
' @local bOk - trial correct
' @local goodCnt - correct trials at this spacing
' @local zeroCnt - trials reading zero at this spacing
' @local v2Cnt - trials with a right first and a wrong second read
' @local excess - elapsed minus the no-stall count
' @local firstExc - trial 0's excess
' @local bExcMixed - trials disagree on excess
' @local firstChar - trial 0's class code
' @local codeChar - this trial's class code
' @local bMixed - trials disagree on class code
' @local cellIdx - arm * 64 + slice * 8 + phase
' @local baseClk - no-stall elapsed count
' @local pShow - record printed in the detail line

  cellIdx := armE * E7_NCELL + sliceIdx * NPHASE + phaseIdx
  repeat distIdx from 0 to E7_NDIST - 1
    baseClk := e7base(armE, distIdx)
    goodCnt := 0
    zeroCnt := 0
    v2Cnt := 0
    bMixed := FALSE
    bExcMixed := FALSE
    pShow := 0
    repeat trialIdx from 0 to TRIALS - 1
      pRec := HUB_E7BUF + ((distIdx * TRIALS + trialIdx) * RECW) * 4
      if long[pRec][REC_EL] == UNWRITTEN
        e7Unwritten++
      cls := e7class(sliceIdx, long[pRec][REC_V1])
      excess := long[pRec][REC_EL] - baseClk
      bOk := cls == C_OK
      codeChar := clschar(cls)
      if armE == AE_B and bOk and long[pRec][REC_V2] <> patnew(sliceIdx + 1)
        bOk := FALSE
        v2Cnt++
        codeChar := "V"
      e7Cls[armE * NCLS + cls]++
      e7Tot[armE]++
      e7ExcMin[armE] <#= excess
      e7ExcMax[armE] #>= excess
      if cls == C_ZERO
        zeroCnt++
      if bOk
        goodCnt++
        e7Good[armE]++
      else
        if pShow == 0
          pShow := pRec
        if e7BadDist[armE] == -1
          e7BadSlice[armE] := sliceIdx
          e7BadPhase[armE] := phaseIdx
          e7BadDist[armE] := distIdx
          e7BadGot[armE] := long[pRec][REC_V1]
      if trialIdx == 0
        firstChar := codeChar
        firstExc := excess
      else
        if codeChar <> firstChar
          bMixed := TRUE
        if excess <> firstExc
          bExcMixed := TRUE
    e7V2Bad[armE] += v2Cnt
    if bMixed
      clsRow[distIdx] := "*"
    else
      clsRow[distIdx] := firstChar
    if bExcMixed
      excRow[distIdx] := "~"
    else
      excRow[distIdx] := excchar(firstExc)
    if goodCnt < TRIALS
      e7BadGaps[cellIdx]++
      e7BadJ[cellIdx] := distIdx
      e7Pure[cellIdx] := zeroCnt == TRIALS and not bExcMixed and firstExc == INSTR_CLK
      ln_s(string("    "))
      ln_e7cell(armE, sliceIdx, phaseIdx)
      ln_s(string(" j"))
      ln_d(distIdx)
      ln_s(string(": ok "))
      ln_d(goodCnt)
      ln_s(string(" zero "))
      ln_d(zeroCnt)
      ln_s(string(" v2bad "))
      ln_d(v2Cnt)
      ln_s(string(" exc "))
      ln_d(firstExc)
      ln_s(string(" mixed "))
      ln_d(bExcMixed & 1)
      ln_s(string(" v1 "))
      ln_h(long[pShow][REC_V1])
      ln_s(string(" v2 "))
      ln_h(long[pShow][REC_V2])
      ln_s(string(" cz "))
      ln_d(long[pShow][REC_FLAGS])
      ln_out()
  clsRow[E7_NDIST] := 0
  excRow[E7_NDIST] := 0
  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_e7cell(armE, sliceIdx, phaseIdx)
  ln_s(string(" cls "))
  ln_s(@clsRow)
  ln_s(string(" exc "))
  say(@excRow)

PRI ln_e7cell(armE, sliceIdx, phaseIdx)
' Append "<arm> s<slice> p<phase>", the lead of every E7 row.
'
' @param armE - E7 arm (AE_*)
' @param sliceIdx - hub slice of the blocking RDFAST's address
' @param phaseIdx - egg-beater phase

  ln_s(e7_name(armE))
  ln_s(string(" s"))
  ln_d(sliceIdx)
  ln_s(string(" p"))
  ln_d(phaseIdx)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' gates
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI is_control(runIdx) : bControl
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bControl - TRUE for C1, PS, C2 (every k), C3, C4; FALSE for T1, T2, T3, T4

  bControl := runIdx < RUN_T1 or runIdx == RUN_C3 or runIdx == RUN_C4

PRI runs_gate() : bPass | runIdx, otherCnt, unwrCnt, disagreeCnt
' Check every image R / W gate; print a RIG FAIL line for each that fails.
' "Other" gates only in the control runs; in a T run it is a result (the
' verdicts report it).  Never-written records gate in every run.
'
' @returns bPass - TRUE when every image R / W gate passed

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run id
' @local otherCnt - X values over the control runs
' @local unwrCnt - never-written records over every image R / W run
' @local disagreeCnt - cells with disagreeing repetitions over every image R / W run

  otherCnt := 0
  unwrCnt := 0
  disagreeCnt := 0
  repeat runIdx from 0 to NRUN - 1
    if is_control(runIdx)
      otherCnt += runOther[runIdx]
    unwrCnt += runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_UNWR]
    disagreeCnt += runDisagree[runIdx]
  bPass := TRUE
  if unwrCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_d(unwrCnt)
    say(string(" image R / W records still hold the fill $EEEE_EEEE: the measuring cog never wrote them"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if runGoodAll[RUN_C1] <> NREC_R
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: C1 (no RDFAST) sentinel in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_C1])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R)
    say(string(" records: the table, the addresses or the read path is wrong"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if runGoodAll[RUN_PS] <> NREC_R
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: PS (positive control) read the stream's first long in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_PS])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R)
    say(string(" records: the RDFAST under test is not shown starting a stream at its address, so a clean T run could not refute anything"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if runGoodAll[RUN_C3] <> NREC_R
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: C3 (no RDFAST) (new,new) in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_C3])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R)
    say(string(" cells: the write path or the read-back is wrong"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if otherCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_d(otherCnt)
    say(string(" values classified X (other) in the control runs C1, PS, C2, C3, C4 - see each run's 'first other value' line"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if disagreeCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_d(disagreeCnt)
    ln_s(string(" image R / W cells whose 16 repetitions disagree - the slot phase was not fixed. T1 primer records over all repetitions: "))
    ln_d(runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" (predicted "))
    ln_d(T1_TOTAL_PRED)
    say(string(")"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if runDamage > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE: "))
    ln_d(runDamage)
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the image R / W runs (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))
  if bPass
    say(string("RIG OK: image R / W - C1 sentinel, PS stream long and C3 (new,new) in every record, no other value in any control run, no record left unwritten, every cell's 16 repetitions identical"))

PRI e7_gate() : bReproduced | cellIdx, gapClk, cellsMatch, noBad, multiBad, outside, impure, phaseIdx, sliceIdx
' Decide whether E7N reproduced Erratum E7's failure; print the evidence.
'
' @returns bReproduced - TRUE when all 64 E7N cells show exactly one E7-shaped failing spacing

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - E7N cell
' @local gapClk - the cell's failing spacing in clocks
' @local cellsMatch - cells in the failure's shape
' @local noBad - cells with no failing spacing
' @local multiBad - cells with more than one failing spacing
' @local outside - cells whose one failing spacing is outside 8..15 clk
' @local impure - cells whose failing spacing was not 16/16 zero with a 2-clk RDFAST
' @local phaseIdx - phase
' @local sliceIdx - slice

  cellsMatch := 0
  noBad := 0
  multiBad := 0
  outside := 0
  impure := 0
  repeat cellIdx from 0 to E7_NCELL - 1
    if e7BadGaps[AE_N * E7_NCELL + cellIdx] == 0
      noBad++
    elseif e7BadGaps[AE_N * E7_NCELL + cellIdx] > 1
      multiBad++
    else
      gapClk := distclk(e7BadJ[AE_N * E7_NCELL + cellIdx])
      if gapClk < E7_GAP_MIN or gapClk > E7_GAP_MAX
        outside++
      elseif not e7Pure[AE_N * E7_NCELL + cellIdx]
        impure++
      else
        cellsMatch++
        gapHist[gapClk - E7_GAP_MIN]++
  repeat phaseIdx from 0 to NPHASE - 1
    repeat sliceIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
      cellIdx := AE_N * E7_NCELL + sliceIdx * NPHASE + phaseIdx
      if e7BadGaps[cellIdx] == 1
        gapClk := distclk(e7BadJ[cellIdx])
        if gapClk <= EXC_DIGIT_MAX
          rowStr[sliceIdx] := "0" + gapClk
        else
          rowStr[sliceIdx] := "A" + gapClk - EXC_LETTER_BASE
      else
        rowStr[sliceIdx] := "?"
    rowStr[NSLOT] := 0
    ln_s(string("  E7N failing spacing at phase "))
    ln_d(phaseIdx)
    ln_s(string(", slices 0-7 (clk: 2-9 digits, A=10 .. K=20, ? = not exactly one): "))
    ln_s(@rowStr)
    ln_s(string("  (expected at this phase: "))
    ln_d(e7Fail[phaseIdx])
    say(string(" clk)"))
  ln_s(string("  E7N cells in the failure's shape by failing spacing: 8 clk "))
  repeat sliceIdx from 0 to E7_GAP_SPAN - 1
    if sliceIdx > 0
      ln_s(string(", "))
      ln_d(E7_GAP_MIN + sliceIdx)
      ln_c(" ")
    ln_d(gapHist[sliceIdx])
  ln_s(string(" (expected: 8 each); E7N wrong "))
  ln_d(e7Tot[AE_N] - e7Good[AE_N])
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(e7Tot[AE_N])
  ln_s(string(", zero "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[AE_N * NCLS + C_ZERO])
  ln_out()
  bReproduced := cellsMatch == E7_NCELL and e7Unwritten == 0
  if e7Unwritten > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_d(e7Unwritten)
    say(string(" E7 records were never written by the measuring cog"))
  if cellsMatch == E7_NCELL
    say(string("POSITIVE CONTROL E7N: REPRODUCED - all 64 cells show exactly one failing spacing in 8..15 clk, 16/16 $0000_0000, blocking RDFAST 2 clk"))
  else
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: E7N positive control did not reproduce the failure - cells in its shape"))
    ln_d(cellsMatch)
    ln_s(string(" of 64; no failing spacing "))
    ln_d(noBad)
    ln_s(string("; more than one "))
    ln_d(multiBad)
    ln_s(string("; outside 8..15 clk "))
    ln_d(outside)
    ln_s(string("; not 16/16 zero with a 2-clk RDFAST "))
    ln_d(impure)
    ln_out()
  if e7Damage > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE: "))
    ln_d(e7Damage)
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the E7 arms (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' verdicts
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI t_cnt(kIdx) : cnt
' @param kIdx - NOP count k
' @returns cnt - repetition-0 primer cells of the no-wait image R run with k NOPs

  cnt := runRep0[(RUN_T1 + kIdx) * NPAIR + VC_PRIM]

PRI delta_match(runIdx, kIdx) : bMatch | deltaIdx
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @param kIdx - NOP count k
' @returns bMatch - TRUE when the run's repetition-0 delta split equals the row

' Local Variables:
' @local deltaIdx - delta 0..7

  bMatch := TRUE
  repeat deltaIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + deltaIdx] <> pred(kIdx, deltaIdx)
      bMatch := FALSE

PRI is_clean(runIdx) : bClean
' @param runIdx - run id (RUN_*)
' @returns bClean - R: sentinel in every record; W: (new,new) in every cell

  bClean := runGoodAll[runIdx] == NREC_R

PRI c2_all_clean() : bClean | kIdx
' @returns bClean - C2 sentinel in every record at every k

' Local Variables:
' @local kIdx - NOP count k

  bClean := TRUE
  repeat kIdx from 0 to KMAX
    if not is_clean(RUN_C2 + kIdx)
      bClean := FALSE

PRI print_window_table() | kIdx, runIdx
' Print the measured early completions per (k, delta) beside the prediction.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local kIdx - NOP count k
' @local runIdx - its no-wait run

  say(string("WINDOW TABLE (no-wait image R, repetition 0, primer cells by delta 0..7 = total | predicted total | C2 at this k: sentinel records of 1024)"))
  repeat kIdx from 0 to KMAX
    runIdx := RUN_T1 + kIdx
    ln_s(string("  k="))
    ln_d(kIdx)
    ln_s(string(": "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" = "))
    ln_d(t_cnt(kIdx))
    ln_s(string(" | "))
    ln_d(predTot[kIdx])
    ln_s(string(" | C2 "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_C2 + kIdx])
    ln_out()

PRI verdict_rdlong(bRunsOk) | primerCnt, seedCnt
' VERDICT E7 RDLONG, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRunsOk - every image R / W gate passed

' Local Variables:
' @local primerCnt - T1 repetition-0 primer cells
' @local seedCnt - T1 seed records over all repetitions

  primerCnt := t_cnt(0)
  seedCnt := runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_SEED]
  if not bRunsOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: NO VERDICT - an image R / W gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
  elseif not is_clean(RUN_C2)
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: INCONCLUSIVE - the waiting-form control C2 k=0 was sentinel in only "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_C2])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 records, so T1's "))
    ln_d(primerCnt)
    say(string(" primer cells are not shown to belong to the no-wait form"))
  elseif seedCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: REFUTED - the early value is not the previous read's: T1 has "))
    ln_d(seedCnt)
    ln_s(string(" seed records (destination never written) over all reps, beside "))
    ln_d(primerCnt)
    say(string(" primer cells per rep"))
  elseif runOther[RUN_T1] > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: REFUTED - the early value is not the previous read's: T1 holds "))
    ln_h(runOtherVal[RUN_T1])
    ln_s(string(" ("))
    ln_d(runOther[RUN_T1])
    ln_s(string(" records), beside "))
    ln_d(primerCnt)
    say(string(" primer cells per rep"))
  elseif runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_STRM] > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: REFUTED - the early value is not the previous read's: T1 holds stream long "))
    ln_h(runStrmVal[RUN_T1])
    ln_s(string(" (data at the RDFAST's address; "))
    ln_d(runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" records), beside "))
    ln_d(primerCnt)
    say(string(" primer cells per rep"))
  elseif primerCnt == 0
    say(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: REFUTED - no early release: T1 read the sentinel in all 64 cells of all 16 repetitions, with C1 and C2 k=0 clean"))
  elseif primerCnt == predTot[0] and delta_match(RUN_T1, 0)
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: CONFIRMED - T1 completed 43 of 64 cells early in every repetition, each reading exactly the primer $A5A5_0001, "))
    say(string("split by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 as predicted; C1 and C2 k=0 sentinel in every record"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDLONG: MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - T1 completed "))
    ln_d(primerCnt)
    ln_s(string(" of 64 cells early in every repetition (predicted 43), each reading exactly the primer $A5A5_0001; by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_T1 * NSLOT])
    say(string(" (predicted 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2)"))

PRI verdict_window(bRunsOk) | kIdx, kZero, totalCnt, seedCnt, bAll, otherCnt, otherVal, strmCnt, strmVal
' VERDICT E7 WINDOW, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRunsOk - every image R / W gate passed

' Local Variables:
' @local kIdx - NOP count k
' @local kZero - smallest k from which every larger k reads zero (KMAX + 1 = beyond the sweep)
' @local totalCnt - primer cells over k = 0..8
' @local seedCnt - seed records over k = 0..8
' @local bAll - every k and delta as predTab
' @local otherCnt - X records over k = 0..8
' @local otherVal - the first X value, from the lowest k that has one
' @local strmCnt - F (stream long) records over k = 0..8
' @local strmVal - the first F value, from the lowest k that has one

  kZero := KMAX + 1
  repeat kIdx from KMAX to 0
    if t_cnt(kIdx) == 0
      kZero := kIdx
    else
      quit
  totalCnt := 0
  seedCnt := 0
  otherCnt := 0
  otherVal := 0
  strmCnt := 0
  strmVal := 0
  bAll := TRUE
  repeat kIdx from 0 to KMAX
    totalCnt += t_cnt(kIdx)
    seedCnt += runCnt[(RUN_T1 + kIdx) * NVC + VC_SEED]
    if otherCnt == 0 and runOther[RUN_T1 + kIdx] > 0
      otherVal := runOtherVal[RUN_T1 + kIdx]
    otherCnt += runOther[RUN_T1 + kIdx]
    if strmCnt == 0 and runCnt[(RUN_T1 + kIdx) * NVC + VC_STRM] > 0
      strmVal := runStrmVal[RUN_T1 + kIdx]
    strmCnt += runCnt[(RUN_T1 + kIdx) * NVC + VC_STRM]
    if t_cnt(kIdx) <> predTot[kIdx] or not delta_match(RUN_T1 + kIdx, kIdx)
      bAll := FALSE
  if not bRunsOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: NO VERDICT - an image R / W gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines)"))
  elseif not c2_all_clean()
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: INCONCLUSIVE - the waiting-form control C2 was not clean at every k (see the WINDOW TABLE C2 column)"))
  elseif seedCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: REFUTED - the early value is not the previous read's: "))
    ln_d(seedCnt)
    say(string(" seed records over T1/T2"))
  elseif otherCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: REFUTED - the early value is not the previous read's: T1/T2 over k=0..8 hold "))
    ln_h(otherVal)
    ln_s(string(" ("))
    ln_d(otherCnt)
    say(string(" records; per-run 'first other value' lines above)"))
  elseif strmCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: REFUTED - the early value is not the previous read's: T1/T2 over k=0..8 hold stream long "))
    ln_h(strmVal)
    ln_s(string(" (data at the RDFAST's address; "))
    ln_d(strmCnt)
    say(string(" records; per-run 'stream longs' lines above)"))
  elseif totalCnt == 0
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: REFUTED - no early release at any k from 0 to 8"))
  elseif bAll
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: CONFIRMED - every k from 0 to 8 and every delta as predicted; zero from k=7 (test RDLONG issued 16 clocks after the RDFAST): "))
    say(string("7 non-hub instructions are a sufficient gap"))
  elseif kZero > KMAX
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - per-k totals in the WINDOW TABLE differ from the prediction, and k=8 still completes early in "))
    ln_d(t_cnt(KMAX))
    say(string(" cells: no sufficient gap within this sweep (predicted zero from k=7)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WINDOW: MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - per-k totals in the WINDOW TABLE differ from the prediction; measured: zero from k="))
    ln_d(kZero)
    ln_s(string(" (test RDLONG issued "))
    ln_d(2 + 2 * kZero)
    say(string(" clocks after the RDFAST) at every larger k; predicted zero from k=7"))

PRI verdict_wrlong(bRunsOk) | base4, cntOO, cntPN, cntNN, cntON, cntDN4, old4, c1Idx
' VERDICT E7 WRLONG, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRunsOk - every image R / W gate passed

' Local Variables:
' @local base4 - T4's first pair counter
' @local cntOO - T3 (old,old) cells
' @local cntPN - T3 (primer,new) cells
' @local cntNN - T3 (new,new) cells
' @local cntON - T3 (old,new) cells
' @local cntDN4 - T4 (seed,new) cells
' @local old4 - T4 cells with rb2 old
' @local c1Idx - rb1 class

  cntOO := runRep0[RUN_T3 * NPAIR + PAIR_OO]
  cntPN := runRep0[RUN_T3 * NPAIR + PAIR_PN]
  cntNN := runRep0[RUN_T3 * NPAIR + PAIR_NN]
  cntON := runRep0[RUN_T3 * NPAIR + PAIR_ON]
  base4 := RUN_T4 * NPAIR
  cntDN4 := runRep0[base4 + PAIR_DN]
  old4 := 0
  repeat c1Idx from 0 to NVC - 1
    old4 += runRep0[base4 + c1Idx * NVC + VC_OLD]
  if not bRunsOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: NO VERDICT - an image R / W gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines)"))
  elseif not is_clean(RUN_C4)
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: INCONCLUSIVE - the waiting-form control C4 was (new,new) in only "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_C4])
    say(string(" of 1024 cells"))
  elseif cntON > 0 or old4 > 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: REFUTED - writes are not lost as predicted: T3 cells (old,new) = write late but landed: "))
    ln_d(cntON)
    ln_s(string("; T4 cells with rb2 old = early WRLONG's write never lands:"))
    ln_d(old4)
    ln_out()
  elseif cntNN == NCELL and cntDN4 == NCELL
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: REFUTED - erratum absent for WRLONG: T3 (new,new) in all 64 cells, T4 (seed,new) in all 64"))
  elseif cntOO + cntPN + cntNN <> NCELL or cntDN4 <> NCELL or cntOO == 0
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: REFUTED - a pattern the prediction does not name (or no (old,old) cell, so no lost write shown): T3 OO "))
    ln_d(cntOO)
    ln_s(string(" PN "))
    ln_d(cntPN)
    ln_s(string(" NN "))
    ln_d(cntNN)
    ln_s(string(" other pairs "))
    ln_d(NCELL - cntOO - cntPN - cntNN)
    ln_s(string("; T4 (seed,new) "))
    ln_d(cntDN4)
    say(string(" of 64 (rows above)"))
  elseif cntOO == T3_PRED_OO and cntPN == T3_PRED_PN and delta_match(RUN_T3, 0)
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: CONFIRMED - T3: 43 cells (old,old) (the write lost), split by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2, and 21 (primer,new) in every repetition; "))
    say(string("T4 (seed,new) in all 64 (the early WRLONG's write lands when nothing follows)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRLONG: MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - T3 (old,old) "))
    ln_d(cntOO)
    ln_s(string(" (predicted 43), (primer,new) "))
    ln_d(cntPN)
    ln_s(string(" (predicted 21), (new,new) "))
    ln_d(cntNN)
    ln_s(string(" (predicted 0); (old,old) by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_T3 * NSLOT])
    say(string("; T4 (seed,new) 64"))

PRI verdict_waiting(bRunsOk) | kIdx, badC2
' VERDICT E7 WAITING FORM, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bRunsOk - every image R / W gate passed

' Local Variables:
' @local kIdx - NOP count k
' @local badC2 - C2 records not sentinel over every k

  badC2 := 0
  repeat kIdx from 0 to KMAX
    badC2 += NREC_R - runGoodAll[RUN_C2 + kIdx]
  if not bRunsOk
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WAITING FORM: NO VERDICT - an image R / W gate failed (see RIG FAIL lines)"))
  elseif badC2 > 0 or not is_clean(RUN_C4)
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WAITING FORM: REFUTED - the waiting form fails: C2 records not sentinel over k=0..8: "))
    ln_d(badC2)
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(NREC_R * (KMAX + 1))
    ln_s(string(" (per k in the WINDOW TABLE); C4 cells not (new,new): "))
    ln_d(NREC_R - runGoodAll[RUN_C4])
    say(string(" of 1024"))
  elseif t_cnt(0) == 0 and runRep0[RUN_T3 * NPAIR + PAIR_NN] == NCELL
    say(string("VERDICT E7 WAITING FORM: INCONCLUSIVE - C2 and C4 were clean, but T1 and T3 did not show the erratum, so the waiting form is not shown beating it"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WAITING FORM: CONFIRMED - C2 sentinel in all 1024 records at every k=0..8 and C4 (new,new) in all 1024 cells, "))
    say(string("in the same run in which the no-wait form completed early"))

PRI verdict_e7b(bReproduced) | clsBase
' VERDICT E7 BLOCKING FIRST, in the order given in the header.
'
' @param bReproduced - E7N reproduced E7 and every E7 record was written

' Local Variables:
' @local clsBase - E7B's first class counter

  clsBase := AE_B * NCLS
  ln_s(string("  E7B by class (first read): ok "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_OK])
  ln_s(string(" stale "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_STALE])
  ln_s(string(" old "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_OLD])
  ln_s(string(" mid "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_MID])
  ln_s(string(" nsh "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_NEWSH])
  ln_s(string(" zero "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_ZERO])
  ln_s(string(" oth "))
  ln_d(e7Cls[clsBase + C_OTHER])
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(e7Tot[AE_B])
  ln_s(string("; right first + wrong second "))
  ln_d(e7V2Bad[AE_B])
  ln_s(string("; two RDFASTs took "))
  ln_d(e7ExcMin[AE_B])
  ln_s(string(".."))
  ln_d(e7ExcMax[AE_B])
  say(string(" clk"))
  if not bReproduced
    say(string("VERDICT E7 BLOCKING FIRST: NO VERDICT - the E7N positive control did not reproduce the failure, or an E7N/E7B record was not written (see RIG FAIL lines)"))
  elseif e7Good[AE_B] < e7Tot[AE_B]
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 BLOCKING FIRST: REFUTED - with the first RDFAST blocking, "))
    ln_d(e7Tot[AE_B] - e7Good[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(e7Tot[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" trials read wrong; first: slice "))
    ln_d(e7BadSlice[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" phase "))
    ln_d(e7BadPhase[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" j "))
    ln_d(e7BadDist[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" first read "))
    ln_h(e7BadGot[AE_B])
    ln_out()
  elseif e7ExcMin[AE_B] < E7B_MIN_EXC
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 BLOCKING FIRST: INCONCLUSIVE - every read was right, but the two RDFASTs took as little as "))
    ln_d(e7ExcMin[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" clk (< "))
    ln_d(E7B_MIN_EXC)
    say(string("): the first RDFAST did not wait in some trial"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 BLOCKING FIRST: CONFIRMED - with the first RDFAST blocking, new[s] then new[s+1] in all "))
    ln_d(e7Tot[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(" trials (64 alignments x 18 spacings x 16), the two RDFASTs taking "))
    ln_d(e7ExcMin[AE_B])
    ln_s(string(".."))
    ln_d(e7ExcMax[AE_B])
    say(string(" clk; E7N in the same run reproduced E7 in 64 of 64 cells"))

DAT ' ---- Fixed predictions (printed in the header before the run) ----
' Predicted early completions (primer cells) per repetition, rows k = 0..8, columns delta 0..7
predTab         long    8, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2          ' k=0  (T1)  43
                long    8, 8, 8, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4          ' k=1        54
                long    8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 7, 6          ' k=2        61
                long    8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8          ' k=3        64
                long    6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6          ' k=4        48
                long    4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4          ' k=5        32
                long    2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2          ' k=6        16
                long    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0          ' k=7         0
                long    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0          ' k=8         0
predTot         long    43, 54, 61, 64, 48, 32, 16, 0, 0
' Erratum E7's failing spacing (clk) at phases 0..7, every slice (informational)
e7Fail          long    10, 9, 8, 15, 14, 13, 12, 11

' ===========================================================================
' MEASURING COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).
' No debug(), no BRK, no interrupt in this cog (DEBUG_COGS excludes it).
' From each primer RDLONG to its test instruction there is nothing but the
' RDFAST (or the NOP standing in for it) and the k NOPs; no ## operand.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Cog ----
pasm            mov     c_tmp, ##STAT_READY
                wrlong  c_tmp, ptra[MB_ALIVE]

wait_cmd        rdlong  c_cmd, ptra                     wz      ' MB_CMD: 0 = idle
        if_z    jmp     #wait_cmd
                rdlong  c_copy, ptra[MB_COPY]
                rdlong  c_mode, ptra[MB_MODE]
                rdlong  c_slice, ptra[MB_SLICE]
                rdlong  c_phase, ptra[MB_PHASE]
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_R                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #run_r
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_W                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #run_w
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_E7                  wz
        if_z    jmp     #run_e7
cmd_done        wrlong  c_mode, ptra[MB_ECHO]                   ' epilogue, after every record: echo the mode run
                wrlong  #0, ptra                                ' MB_CMD := 0 -> done
                jmp     #wait_cmd

'--- image R: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 ar; record (rep*8 + af)*8 + ar
run_r           alts    c_copy, #rvec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0
                mov     c_rp, c_res
                mov     c_reps, #REPS
r_rep           mov     c_af, #0
r_af            mov     c_ar, #0
r_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm                            ' stream address: slot bits = af
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tbl                             ' test address: slot bits = ar
                mov     c_dst, c_seedv                          ' "never written" stays visible
                jmp     c_vec                                   ' the trial copy
r_settle        mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
r_dly           djnz    c_t, #r_dly                             ' >= 200 clocks: everything settles
                wrlong  c_dst, c_rp                             ' one record per trial
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_af
                djnz    c_reps, #r_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image R trial copies: primer, RDFAST (or NOP), k NOPs, the RDLONG under test
r_nop           rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' C1: primer
                nop                                             ' C1: NOP in place of the RDFAST
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                             ' C1: the RDLONG under test
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k0            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' k=0: primer
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' k=0: the stream under test
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                             ' k=0: the RDLONG under test
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k1            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k2            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k3            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k4            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k5            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k6            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k7            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_k8            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
r_strm          rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' PS: primer
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' PS: the stream under test (no-wait)
                waitx   #STREAM_WAIT                            ' PS: long past any start-up
                rflong  c_dst                                   ' PS: the stream's first long
                jmp     #r_settle

'--- image W: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 aw; records rb1, rb2 per trial
run_w           alts    c_copy, #wvec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0
                mov     c_rp, c_res
                mov     c_reps, #REPS
w_rep           mov     c_af, #0
w_af            mov     c_ar, #0                                ' c_ar = aw: the target's slot bits
w_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm                            ' stream address: slot bits = af
                mov     c_pw, c_ar
                shl     c_pw, #2
                add     c_pw, c_wtbl                            ' write target: slot bits = aw
                wrlong  c_oldv, c_pw                            ' the target holds the old value
                mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
w_d1            djnz    c_t, #w_d1
                mov     c_rb1, c_seedv
                mov     c_rb2, c_seedv
                jmp     c_vec                                   ' the trial copy
w_settle        mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
w_d2            djnz    c_t, #w_d2
                rdlong  c_rb2, c_pw                             ' read-back after everything settled
                wrlong  c_rb1, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_rb2, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #w_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #w_af
                djnz    c_reps, #w_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image W trial copies
w_nop           rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' C3: primer
                nop                                             ' C3: NOP in place of the RDFAST
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw                            ' C3: the WRLONG under test
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pw                             ' C3: immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle
w_w1            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' C4/T3: primer
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' C4/T3: the stream under test
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw                            ' C4/T3: the WRLONG under test
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pw                             ' C4/T3: immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle
w_w2            rdlong  c_tmp, c_prim                           ' T4: primer
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' T4: the stream under test
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw                            ' T4: the WRLONG under test
                nop                                             ' T4: no immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle

'--- E7 arms: per (slice, phase), 18 spacings x 16 trials; record el, v1, v2, flags
run_e7          mov     c_hubn, c_slice
                shl     c_hubn, #2
                add     c_hubn, c_e7new                         ' blocking RDFAST: new[s]
                mov     c_bufp, c_e7buf
                mov     c_dist, #0
e_dist          mov     c_dly, c_dist
                cmp     c_dist, #0                      wz
        if_nz   sub     c_dly, #1                               ' j >= 1: WAITX c_dly = j - 1
                mov     c_trial, #TRIALS
e_trial         call    #prelude
                tjnz    c_dist, #e_seqn
e_seq0          rdlong  c_junk, c_e7old                         ' egg-beater sync (slice 0)
                waitx   c_phase
                getct   c_t0
                rdfast  c_mode, c_hubf                          ' first RDFAST: E7N D[31]=1, E7B D=0
                rdfast  #0, c_hubn                              ' blocking RDFAST, spacing index 0
                rflong  c_r1                            wcz
                getct   c_t1
                wrc     c_r3
                bitz    c_r3, #FLAG_Z_BIT
                rflong  c_r2
                jmp     #e_post
e_seqn          rdlong  c_junk, c_e7old                         ' egg-beater sync (slice 0)
                waitx   c_phase
                getct   c_t0
                rdfast  c_mode, c_hubf                          ' first RDFAST: E7N D[31]=1, E7B D=0
                waitx   c_dly                                   ' the spacing
                rdfast  #0, c_hubn                              ' blocking RDFAST
                rflong  c_r1                            wcz
                getct   c_t1
                wrc     c_r3
                bitz    c_r3, #FLAG_Z_BIT
                rflong  c_r2
e_post          mov     c_r0, c_t1
                sub     c_r0, c_t0                              ' elapsed
                setq    #RECW - 1
                wrlong  c_r0, c_bufp                            ' record: c_r0..c_r3
                add     c_bufp, #RECW * 4
                djnz    c_trial, #e_trial
                add     c_dist, #1
                cmp     c_dist, #E7_NDIST               wz
        if_nz   jmp     #e_dist
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- PRIME the FIFO with the OLD region
prelude         rdfast  #0, c_e7old                             ' blocking RDFAST of old[]
                waitx   #PRIME_WAIT
                rflong  c_junk                                  ' consume old[0]
                rflong  c_junk                                  ' consume old[1]: FIFO next = old[2]
                waitx   #SETTLE_WAIT                            ' FIFO refills and idles
                ret

'--- trial-copy vectors
rvec_tab        long    r_k0, r_k1, r_k2, r_k3, r_k4, r_k5, r_k6, r_k7, r_k8         ' index k = 0..8
                long    r_nop, r_strm                                                 ' COPY_RNOP = 9, COPY_RSTRM = 10
wvec_tab        long    w_nop, w_w1, w_w2                                             ' COPY_WNOP, COPY_W1, COPY_W2

'--- cog data
c_strm          long    HUB_STRM
c_tbl           long    HUB_TBL
c_wtbl          long    HUB_WTBL
c_prim          long    HUB_PRIM
c_res           long    HUB_RES
c_e7new         long    HUB_E7NEW
c_e7old         long    HUB_E7OLD
c_hubf          long    HUB_E7MID                               ' E7 first RDFAST address: mid[0]
c_e7buf         long    HUB_E7BUF
c_seedv         long    SEEDV
c_oldv          long    OLDV
c_newv          long    NEWV
c_r0            long    0                                       ' E7 record c_r0..c_r3 -- MUST stay contiguous
c_r1            long    0
c_r2            long    0
c_r3            long    0
c_cmd           long    0
c_copy          long    0
c_mode          long    0                                       ' RDFAST D under test
c_slice         long    0
c_phase         long    0
c_vec           long    0
c_rp            long    0
c_reps          long    0
c_af            long    0
c_ar            long    0
c_pf            long    0
c_pr            long    0
c_pw            long    0
c_dst           long    0
c_rb1           long    0
c_rb2           long    0
c_t             long    0
c_tmp           long    0
c_hubn          long    0
c_bufp          long    0
c_dist          long    0
c_dly           long    0
c_trial         long    0
c_t0            long    0
c_t1            long    0
c_junk          long    0
pasm_end

